# Rules

## General

- Save tokens, be concrete, no fluff.
- Ask before destructive operations (install, file deletion, config changes). Safe commands (git status, read) run without asking.
- The app and CSS watcher are already running (`start_app.ps1` + Tailwind watch window). Do not start or rebuild them automatically. If something does not work, ask for a manual start/restart.
- Dev: <http://pulsedeck.lan:8005/> (`deploy/.env.dev`, `UVICORN_HOST=0.0.0.0` — DNS `.lan` → LAN IP, not 127.0.0.1).
- Never run tests yourself — point out how to run them manually.
- Windows environment — commands in PowerShell.

- Before finishing: rethink the implementation — simplify as far as reasonable (reuse or add shared helpers if that shortens the result), then strip leftovers. Do not stop at "it works".

## URL (public / portal)

- No UUIDs in UI links. Project: `/p/{key}`, ticket: `/t/{key}-{number}` (number per project, from 1).
- Helpers: `app/utils/urls.py` (`project_path`, `ticket_path`, `ticket_label`, `admin_project_path`).
- Project `key`: manual `[A-Z0-9]{1,5}`, unique; name independent, unique case-insensitive.
- Key/name change without redirects — old links stop working.
- In DB: all entities have bigint PK (autoincrement). Project key and `ticket.number` only for routing and labels.

## Forms / CSRF

- Session POST requires `X-CSRF-Token` (meta + interceptor in `base.html` or `hx-headers`).
- Form interceptor: `fetch` with `redirect: "follow"` (not `manual` — causes a blank page).
- After success with redirect: navigate to `r.url` when `r.redirected`.

## Code

- Log errors in key operations and try/except.
- Secure code resistant to known attacks.
- No comments (unless the user requires them). Structural CSS section banners `/* === … === */` are allowed.
- Never edit `frontend/static/css/app.css` — generated (`css:watch` / `css:build`).
- Reuse existing styles — consistency before new CSS.
- KISS / YAGNI / DRY; SOLID when it makes sense, no over-architecture.

## CSS/UI

- Tailwind + custom components in `_components.css` (`.btn`, `.input`, `.modal`…). Avoid unnecessary custom CSS and inline styles.
- First look for an existing component / class in `_components.css` / `_primitives.css`, then combine Tailwind classes.
- Use colors from `@theme` (`bg-primary`, `text-secondary`, `bg-base-100`).
- Banery sekcji `/* === … === */` w CSS są dozwolone; innych komentarzy unikać.

## Themes / CSS tokens

- Osie: `data-theme` = paleta; `data-scheme` = light/dark depth; `data-theme-gradient` = on (głębia) / off (płaski).
- Palety: zachować hexy `--color-*` i charakter `--page/aside/rail-gradient`; depth/btn wolno uspójniać.
- Komponenty: tła/cienie przycisków przez `var(--btn-bg-*)` / `var(--btn-shadow-*)`; nie hardcodować nowych glow/gradientów btn.
- Nowa para motywów: wpis w `THEME_PAIRS` + `_THEMES` + paleta w `_themes.css` + i18n (drugi ID w parze = dark, `DARK_THEME_IDS` liczone automatycznie).
- Nie edytować `frontend/static/css/app.css` — generated (`css:watch` / `css:build`).

## Stack

Backend: FastAPI + SQLAlchemy + PostgreSQL + Alembic. CSS: Tailwind + custom components. Start: `start_app.ps1`, npm: `update_npm.ps1`.

## Network

- Do not fetch full HTML pages — the user pastes data manually.
- Allowed: checking HTTP status and headers.
- Browser only on explicit request or a short test (<50 lines).
